when star wars the clone wars was  revived for a final season on disney  plus  fans of the series were ecstatic little  did they know they'd also be getting a  whole new follow-up series in star wars  the bad badge let's break down the first  episode of this new star wars chapter  first off order 66 everyone remembers  the infamous  order 66. what's order 66  also known as clone protocol 66 this is  a sith created order that brands jedi as  traders and subjects them to  execution emperor palpatine activates  this early on in the episode forcing the  bad batch to watch in horror as the rest  of the clone troops massacre the jedi  the sudden betrayal of the jedi plunges  the bad batch crew wrecker hunter echo  tech and crosshair into the universe's  brand new status quo as the republic  transitions into darth sidious galactic  empire it's later explained that the  genetic abnormalities of clone force  99's members mean their  inhibitor chips don't work properly  which instantly puts them at odds with  the rest of the imperial forces  the defective clones with the desirable  mutations  unfortunately their situation only gets  more desperate when grand moff tarkin  arrives on the aquatic planet kamino to  assess whether the empire really needs a  clone army choosing to investigate the  bad batch and their unique fighting  style but when they're dispatched to the  onderon sector under the pretense of  killing separatist insurgents the  batbatcher faced with a horrifying  realization  they were actually sent to kill republic  men women and children who disagree with  the empire and its fascist grip on the  galaxy  thankfully because the bad batch's chips  don't work they can't face carrying out  their mission rightfully choosing to  disobey their orders instead once again  it proves that their individual  personalities are their true strengths  in a fight of good vs evil  but it also means they failed the test  that tarkin set out for them will their  disobedience be the catalyst for the  empire ditching the clones for  conscripted civilians  quite possibly but we'll have to wait to  see in future episodes  unfortunately for the team there's one  soldier among them who isn't quite as  down with disobeying orders  good soldiers  unlike the other mutant clones crosshair  still wants to carry out the missions  he's been given even attempting to shoot  a jedi padawan in the introduction of  the bad batch episode 1. he constantly  butts heads with hunter the bad batch's  leader over the group not sticking to  their orders acting more like a typical  clone than  any of the others during the ondrawn  mission it becomes clearer that  crosshair's chip is still functioning to  some degree  as he votes to execute all the republic  outlaws it's likely that because his  genetics make his sharp shooting skills  even sharper they  also make him more amenable to taking  orders because of the sheer focus  required to be a sniper crosshair has to  be detached from the idea of killing  because he picks his targets off from a  distance which also explains why he has  such a cold  demeanor to make matters worse tarkin  and the kaminoans put crosshair's chip  into overdrive which forces him to fight  his own teammates during their escape  from the cloning facility he doesn't  exactly hold back  either directly taking aim at their  heads one shot nearly takes record down  crosshair even fires upon the innocent  clone child omega which perfectly  encapsulates just how far off the deep  end he's gone  luckily the team escapes from kamino  without crosshair and with omega but  thanks to crosshair's newfound loyalty  to tarkin and the empire it probably  isn't the last we've seen of them  right after the bad batch returns to  kamino we're introduced to omega a  mysterious young girl who also happens  to be a clone she's working under the  kaminoans as some kind of medical  apprentice although it's not exactly  clear why  because of the bad batch's unique  appearances and behavior omega instantly  feels a certain kinship with them  after all she's surrounded by thousands  of faces that all look the same  and yet has no one to connect with aside  from a helpful droid it's perfectly  understandable why omega is drawn to the  bad batch they're like her  that's the main reason why she leaves  kamino with them just like there's  nothing on kamino for the bad batch  anymore there's nothing there for omega  either as she points out she's never  been anywhere except the cloning  facility which makes flying around in a  spaceship  incredibly exciting the moment in the  cockpit where hunter watches as omega's  eyes widen at light speed travel shows  just how empathetic and compassionate  the clones can be  the relationship between an innocent  child like omega and the hardened  soldiers of the bad batch crew  also adds an excellent dynamic to the  series one that we've seen work wonders  in the star wars universe before  looking ahead both omega and the bad  batch will be forced to grow and develop  in new ways because of their partnership  omega's naivete will push the bad batch  to be even more empathetic and steady in  their convictions and the bad batches  boldness bravery and connections to  people in places all over the galaxy  will open omega up to a whole new life  where have we seen that before the  mandalorian would like a word  now that the bad batch have been branded  as traders they can no longer call  kamino their home  sparking a brand new adventure for them  to embark on but this raises a number of  questions  since they all have similar facial  features to other clones it's going to  be very difficult keeping a low profile  among the current imperial forces  because they'll be instantly  recognizable  this is likely why they're seeking help  from an old friend as hunter puts it but  it's not quite clear who it is they're  looking for  while it would be easy to assume that  they're looking for commander rex since  the squad worked alongside him in the  clone wars season seven  it's not that simple the bad batch has  no way of knowing if his chip has forced  rex into an imperial minion or not and  it would be a big gamble to just assume  that he'd be able and willing to help  them in a post-order 66 world whoever  hunter's friend  is they live in sector j19 also called  the seleucomy system  the sector was seen way back in the  clone wars season 2 where a clone  deserter named cutler queen lives a  peaceful life on a farm  could this be the person the bad batch  is going to meet up with it's not  impossible that dave filoni and the star  wars the bad batch writers are calling  back to earlier plots and characters in  the series over the course of this new  show but only time will reveal who's  going to ally with the squad  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  star wars are coming soon subscribe to  our youtube channel and hit the bell so  you don't miss a single one
 

